<title>RUSSIA: Russian govt targets higher domestic grain buying.</title>
<headline>Russian govt targets higher domestic grain buying.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian government intends to buy 4.9 million tonnes of grain for its Federal Food Corporation's strategic reserves in 1997, according to a resolution.</p>
<p>The target, cited by Interfax news agency, is for grain reserves used to feed the military and other special consumers.</p>
<p>The newly reorganised Corporation performed poorly last year and managed to buy only 415,000 tonnes of grain, nine percent of its target of 4.5 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Russia also has strategic grain reserves variously known as GosFond or the Federal Fund, but their size is a state secret.</p>
<p>Moscow has said it will buy only domestic grain for the military.</p>
<p>Last year's net grain harvest of 69.3 million tonnes was the second poor result in a row.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
